率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":2.5,"default_fair_val":2.5,"premium_pct":249.6,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":63.8,"pe_forward":56.1,"pb_trailing":6.5,"pb_forward":5.9,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":13.8,"fcf_to_ev":1.86,"fcf_to_mcap":1.81,"liab_to_assets":37.3,"cash_to_assets":29.9,"current_ratio":2.38,"roe":10.2,"roa":6.4,"moat":null,"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":"analysisUnavailable"},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-02-28","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T06:23:22.835Z","evidenceHash":"d58cb0dfcb113ea69b1dec15380073ba335c60fa3d61377ebc52617f6d37932f"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-02-28","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T06:23:22.835Z","evidenceHash":"d58cb0dfcb113ea69b1dec15380073ba335c60fa3d61377ebc52617f6d37932f"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/BB.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/BB.png","website":"https://web.blackberry.com","ceo":"John Joseph Giamatteo","full_time_employees":"1749","description":"BlackBerry Limited stands as a global technology company, delivering intelligent security solutions, software, and comprehensive services to government bodies and businesses worldwide. Its operational structure is divided into three primary segments: Cybersecurity, Internet of Things (IoT), and Licensing & Other ventures. Within its Cybersecurity division, the company offers the sophisticated BlackBerry Cyber Suite. This platform leverages Cylance's artificial intelligence and machine learning capabilities to provide a robust array of protective measures. Key components include BlackBerry Protect, an Endpoint Protection Platform (EPP) also featuring Mobile Threat Defense (MTD); BlackBerry Optics, an Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) solution designed for deep visibility and proactive prevention of malicious activities; BlackBerry Guard, which delivers managed detection and response (MDR) services; BlackBerry Gateway, an AI-driven Zero Trust Network Access (ZTNA) offering; and BlackBerry Persona, a User and Entity Behavior Analytics (UEBA) solution focused on real-time user identity verification. Beyond its core cybersecurity offerings, BlackBerry provides the Spark Unified Endpoint Management (UEM) Suite. This suite encompasses BlackBerry UEM, serving as the foundational software for its secure communication ecosystem, and BlackBerry Dynamics, which furnishes a secure container technology and development environment for mobile applications. The company further supplies critical event management systems such as BlackBerry AtHoc and BlackBerry Alert. For government entities, it offers SecuSUITE, a secure voice and text messaging solution compatible across multiple operating systems, alongside BBM Enterprise, a secure instant messaging platform tailored for corporate use. In the sphere of embedded systems and the IoT, BlackBerry’s diverse portfolio includes BlackBerry QNX, recognized for its Neutrino operating system, the BlackBerry QNX CAR platform, and various embedded solutions. Other notable products are BlackBerry Jarvis, a cloud-native platform for static application security testing of binaries; BlackBerry Certicom, specializing in cryptographic and management products; BlackBerry Radar, an asset monitoring solution; and BlackBerry IVY, an intelligent vehicle data platform. These are complemented by a suite of enterprise and cybersecurity consulting services. Furthermore, BlackBerry generates revenue through its substantial patent licensing program and fees derived from access to legacy services. Founded in 1984, BlackBerry Limited is strategically headquartered in Waterloo, Canada.","description_en":"BlackBerry Limited stands as a global technology company, delivering intelligent security solutions, software, and comprehensive services to government bodies and businesses worldwide. Its operational structure is divided into three primary segments: Cybersecurity, Internet of Things (IoT), and Licensing & Other ventures. Within its Cybersecurity division, the company offers the sophisticated BlackBerry Cyber Suite. This platform leverages Cylance's artificial intelligence and machine learning capabilities to provide a robust array of protective measures. Key components include BlackBerry Protect, an Endpoint Protection Platform (EPP) also featuring Mobile Threat Defense (MTD); BlackBerry Optics, an Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) solution designed for deep visibility and proactive prevention of malicious activities; BlackBerry Guard, which delivers managed detection and response (MDR) services; BlackBerry Gateway, an AI-driven Zero Trust Network Access (ZTNA) offering; and BlackBerry Persona, a User and Entity Behavior Analytics (UEBA) solution focused on real-time user identity verification. Beyond its core cybersecurity offerings, BlackBerry provides the Spark Unified Endpoint Management (UEM) Suite. This suite encompasses BlackBerry UEM, serving as the foundational software for its secure communication ecosystem, and BlackBerry Dynamics, which furnishes a secure container technology and development environment for mobile applications. The company further supplies critical event management systems such as BlackBerry AtHoc and BlackBerry Alert. For government entities, it offers SecuSUITE, a secure voice and text messaging solution compatible across multiple operating systems, alongside BBM Enterprise, a secure instant messaging platform tailored for corporate use. In the sphere of embedded systems and the IoT, BlackBerry’s diverse portfolio includes BlackBerry QNX, recognized for its Neutrino operating system, the BlackBerry QNX CAR platform, and various embedded solutions. Other notable products are BlackBerry Jarvis, a cloud-native platform for static application security testing of binaries; BlackBerry Certicom, specializing in cryptographic and management products; BlackBerry Radar, an asset monitoring solution; and BlackBerry IVY, an intelligent vehicle data platform. These are complemented by a suite of enterprise and cybersecurity consulting services. Furthermore, BlackBerry generates revenue through its substantial patent licensing program and fees derived from access to legacy services. Founded in 1984, BlackBerry Limited is strategically headquartered in Waterloo, Canada.","description_zh":"BlackBerry Limited（美股代碼：BB）為 Technology 領域之重要企業，專注於 Software - Infrastructure 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"2200 University Avenue East","city":"Waterloo","state":"ON","zip":"N2K 0A7","country":"CA","phone":"15198887465","full_address":"2200 University Avenue East, Waterloo, ON N2K 0A7, CA","range_52w":"3.12-13.59","year_high":13.59,"year_low":3.12,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":3.12,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-11-05","name":"Chaikof David","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":5000,"price":8.18,"total_val":0.04},{"date":"2026-10-30","name":"Chaikof David","title":"director: ","is_buy":null,"action":"","shares":0,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"GIAMATTEO JOHN JOSEPH","title":"director, officer: CEO & President, Secure Comm.","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":151000,"price":9.4,"total_val":1.42},{"date":"2026-10-22","name":"GIAMATTEO JOHN JOSEPH","title":"director, officer: CEO & President, Secure Comm.","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":99000,"price":8.74,"total_val":0.87},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Armstrong-Owen Jennifer","title":"officer: Sr VP & Chief People Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":7636,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Armstrong-Owen